{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0157o6u2LQjdMhd1Ud2XX199","type":"tool_result","content":"25:{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"create\",\"name\":\"bench\",\"asset\":{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"bench\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\"description\":\"A wooden bench, its backrest leaning on the rear legs.\",\"materials\":{\"wood\":{\"color\":\"#bc8150\"},\"wood_dark\":{\"color\":\"#594635\"}},\"parts\":{\"seat\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,18,76],\"radius\":2.5,\"pos\":[0,80,0],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"backrest\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,8],\"radius\":2.5,\"from\":[0,92,-38],\"to\":[0,141,-48],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"leg_front\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,0,25],\"to\":[85,71,25],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"leg_back\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,1,-26],\"to\":[85,141,-56],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"crossbar\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6],\"from\":[-80,31,-33],\"to\":[80,31,-33],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\"}},\"sockets\":{\"sit\":{\"pos\":[0,89,4]}}}}}\n62:the field guide (also tags, category, spin, sway, segments, half, half_height, remap, source, fit,\n# Object Studio\n\nObjects (props) are JSON documents of named parts. A command is one line, `tool key=value ...`\nor `{\"tool\":\"…\",\"args\":{…}}`; keep it on that line, document and all: a line break splits it\ninto broken commands.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. `assets find=words` finds a starting point: templates (BUILTIN/box, crate, bench, lantern),\n   library packs (LIB/pack/name, read-only: copy one; imported packs: docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md) and\n   saved objects (WORKSHOP/name). Rows are name cat size_cm tier mesh tok tags desc, best first\n   (tier: standard, checked or disk; mesh: % read-only mesh); a miss says `none` with a route;\n   filters `category=`, `tags=` (`@sit`: a socket), `tier=standard` (what every build has),\n   `similar=NAME`; `next` pages.\n2. Make the object and look at it in one go: a create command like the one below and, on the\n   next line, `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`. The create reply has size_cm and\n   check (what is wrong); the preview writes a sheet of four views beside a 1.8 m figure, the\n   image to look at (the reply's path; no capture needed).\n3. If the check or the sheet shows a fault, fix it in one more go: a patch (below) and a new\n   sheet. Otherwise stop; the first go is often the whole job.\nPACK.json\naltar.json\nanvil.json\naxe.json\nbanner.json\n62\n{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"park_bench\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\n\"description\":\"A park bench of three seat slats and two back slats between dark frames with armrests; seats three.\",\n\"tags\":[\"bench\",\"seat\",\"wood\",\"park\",\"town\",\"village\"],\n\"category\":\"furniture\",\n\"lineage\":{\"method\":\"edited\",\"origin\":\"import\",\"parents\":[\"LIB/quaternius_medieval_village/bench_1@prop2-14c863f487a932ef\"],\"license\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"credit\":\"Quaternius (quaternius.com)\"},\n\"source\":{\"library\":\"quaternius/medieval_village\",\"license\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"title\":\"Bench_1\"},\n\"materials\":{\n\"frame\":{\"color\":\"#4e3420\"},\n\"slat\":{\"base\":\"MAT/oak_planks\",\"color\":\"#8a5e3a\"}},\n\"parts\":{\n\"arm\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[7,4,46],\"radius\":1,\"pos\":[93,66,-3],\"mat\":\"frame\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\n\"back\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[180,10,3],\"radius\":1,\"pos\":[0,66,-24],\"pitch\":-10,\"mat\":\"slat\",\"array\":{\"count\":2,\"step\":[0,15,-2.6]}},\n\"leg\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6],\"from\":[93,0,14],\"to\":[93,64,14],\"mat\":\"frame\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\n\"post\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6],\"from\":[93,0,-17],\"to\":[93,84,-28],\"mat\":\"frame\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\n\"rail\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6,40],\"pos\":[93,37,-2],\"mat\":\"frame\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\n\"seat\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[190,4,11],\"radius\":1,\"pos\":[0,42,0],\"mat\":\"slat\",\"array\":{\"count\":3,\"step\":[0,0,12.5]}}},\n\"sockets\":{\n\"sit\":{\"pos\":[0,44,0]}},\n\"params\":{\n\"length\":{\"range\":[80,320],\"set\":{\"arm.pos.0\":0.4895,\"back.size.0\":0.9474,\"leg.from.0\":0.4895,\"leg.to.0\":0.4895,\"post.from.0\":0.4895,\"post.to.0\":0.4895,\"rail.pos.0\":0.4895,\"seat.size.0\":1}}},\n\"presets\":{\n\"long\":{\"length\":300},\n\"short\":{\"length\":110}}}\ncrates/pav_core/src/props/index.rs:255:        [\"templates/index.tsv\", \"lib/core/index.tsv\"]\ncrates/pav_core/src/props/index.rs:279:/// The folders of the packs on disk under `root`: (pack, folder, tier). `lib/core` is\ncrates/pav_core/src/props/mesh.rs:14://! the core pack (`core/<name>`) in the files every build embeds (`lib/core/meshes/`), then on\ncrates/pav_core/src/props/mesh.rs:213:/// The text of an embedded mesh: the core pack's (`core/<name>`, from `lib/core/meshes/`).\ncrates/pav_core/src/props/mesh.rs:216:    (pack == super::store::CORE).then(|| super::store::embedded_file(&format!(\"lib/core/meshes/{leaf}.json\")))?\ncrates/pav_core/src/catalogue.rs:78:/// templates, then `LIB/core`), then the committed packs under the props root, then the shipped\ncrates/pav_core/src/figure.rs:247:    /// The body prop, `LIB/<pack>/<name>`.\ncrates/pav_core/src/figure.rs:500:    /// The body's name, `LIB/<pack>/<name>`.\ncrates/pav_core/src/figure.rs:598:/// The figure `name` (`LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight`): installed, else read once from its\ncrates/pav_core/src/figure.rs:807:            body: \"LIB/test_figures/t\".into(),\ncrates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs:58:    /// A library prop drawn in place of the weapon (`LIB/core/mage_staff`), held by its `grip`\ncrates/pav_core/src/puppet.rs:233:    /// An imported figure drawn in place of the puppet's parts (`LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight`,\ncrates/pav_core/src/store.rs:19:    /// Its asset name (`LIB/core/x` or `BUILTIN/x`).\ncrates/pav_core/src/store.rs:219:    /// The set or pack, e.g. `STYLE100` or `LIB/core`; `where_` says where it lives.\ncrates/pav_core/src/