{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HCy8hg2pf8PiTpgmzjMTqi","type":"tool_result","content":"    Finished `dev` profile [optimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 19.17s\ncrates/pav_tools/src/bridge.rs:7://!   -> {\"id\": 1, \"tool\": \"capture\", \"args\": {\"width\": 640}}\ncrates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs:83:        name: \"capture\",\n14:  capture    Render a screenshot (PNG) with the software/real GPU.  out=<string> width=<integer> height=<integer> stats=<string> ui=<boolean>\n16:  gpu        Describe the GPU adapter used for captures.  \n40:  audio_capture Run N ticks (optionally driving the player) and render the game's sounds to a .wav file.  ticks=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> out=<string>\n64:  mocap      Open motion-capture databases, translated on demand; no args lists them. find=WORDS searches takes; get=IDS downloads (cmu: all); cut=TAKE fits a moment into a set. survey= measures or translates CMU takes.  find=<string> lib=<string> get=<string> survey=<string> subjects=<string> cut=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> name=<string> set=<string> tags=<string> desc=<string> tol=<number> limit=<integer> out=<string>\n67:  anim_preview View an animation in an isolated studio with the game's renderer; the game resumes when it closes. clip=SET/Clip or move=NAME. Same-name edits keep the clock and camera. No args: preview state; action=pose: the sampled pose. capture/filmstrip show the studio.  clip=<string> move=<string> playing=<boolean> time=<number> step=<integer> speed=<number> repeat=<boolean> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> side=<number> hit=<number> action=<string> close=<boolean>\n72:  creature_edit Create and revise procedural rigged creatures: create (bundled template, blueprint or seeded theme), patch (atomic named-path SpawnForge ops), surface (skin), copy, inspect, replace, undo, redo, rebuild. Pass if_revision from inspect or the last job. Builds are asynchronous: poll creature_status until published or failed before judging a capture; a failed or superseded job keeps the last good stage. The CLI waits.  action=<string> name=<string> template=<string> theme=<string> seed=<integer> constraints=<object> blueprint=<object> from=<string> quality=<string> ops=<array> skin=<object> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean>\n{\"height\":720,\"path\":\"../notes/cap/title.png\",\"render_ms\":648,\"tick\":120,\"width\":1280}\n{\"height\":720,\"path\":\"../notes/cap/island.png\",\"render_ms\":664,\"tick\":60,\"width\":1280}\n{\"height\":720,\"path\":\"../notes/cap/pose.png\",\"render_ms\":617,\"tick\":200,\"width\":1280}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb437ba7-0477-4143-bb04-ff33f49efd62","uuid":"55373f29-d107-4de3-8610-8ef45e613484","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:33:10.069Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    Finished `dev` profile [optimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 19.17s\ncrates/pav_tools/src/bridge.rs:7://!   -> {\"id\": 1, \"tool\": \"capture\", \"args\": {\"width\": 640}}\ncrates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs:83:        name: \"capture\",\n14:  capture    Render a screenshot (PNG) with the software/real GPU.  out=<string> width=<integer> height=<integer> stats=<string> ui=<boolean>\n16:  gpu        Describe the GPU adapter used for captures.  \n40:  audio_capture Run N ticks (optionally driving the player) and render the game's sounds to a .wav file.  ticks=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> out=<string>\n64:  mocap      Open motion-capture databases, translated on demand; no args lists them. find=WORDS searches takes; get=IDS downloads (cmu: all); cut=TAKE fits a moment into a set. survey= measures or translates CMU takes.  find=<string> lib=<string> get=<string> survey=<string> subjects=<string> cut=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> name=<string> set=<string> tags=<string> desc=<string> tol=<number> limit=<integer> out=<