{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjMdi2uBPHwhqvCNjaFF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01319uzD5eq45pp85z6qxZbn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261104-223953__x35112d/work/WeStand-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953\npython3 - <<'PY'\ndef sub(path, old, new, count=1):\n    s=open(path).read()\n    assert old in s, (path, old[:60])\n    s=s.replace(old,new,count)\n    open(path,'w').write(s)\nsub('engine/crates/pav_core/src/parts.rs','''                let base = a.center + u * a.back_r * 0.72;\n                let w = a.back_r * 0.62 * s;\n                let n = 9;\n                let at = |i: i32| {\n                    let th = std::f32::consts::PI * i as f32 / n as f32;\n                    base + r * (th.cos() * w) + u * (th.sin() * w * 1.25)\n                };\n                for i in 0..n {\n                    push(at(i), at(i + 1), a.back_r * 0.13 * s, a.back_r * 0.13 * s, c, g);\n                }''','''                // The ball's radius, whatever the body reports: the handle stands well clear of it.\n                let ball = a.back_r.max(0.3 * a.k);\n                let base = a.center + u * ball * 0.75;\n                let w = ball * 0.68 * s;\n                let n = 11;\n                let at = |i: i32| {\n                    let th = std::f32::consts::PI * i as f32 / n as f32;\n                    base + r * (th.cos() * w) + u * (th.sin() * w * 1.1)\n                };\n                for i in 0..n {\n                    push(at(i), at(i + 1), ball * 0.17 * s, ball * 0.17 * s, c, g);\n                }''')\nM='engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/ui_model.rs'\nsub(M,'''    /// A name above a figure.''','''    /// A ring on the ground around what the mouse points at.\n    WorldRing { at: [f32; 3], r: f32 },\n    /// A name above a figure.''')\nU='engine/crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs'\nsub(U,'''            Ui::WorldLabel { at, text: s } => {''','''            Ui::WorldRing { at, r } => {\n                let project = |w: [f32; 3]| {\n                    let v = vp * Vec4::new(w[0], w[1], w[2], 1.0);\n                    (v.w > 0.0).then(|| {\n                        let n = v.truncate() / v.w;\n                        pos2((n.x * 0.5 + 0.5) * sp.size.x, (0.5 - n.y * 0.5) * sp.size.y)\n                    })\n                };\n                // Round the ring by points on the ground.\n                let pts: Vec<Pos2> = (0..28)\n                    .filter_map(|i| {\n                        let a = i as f32 / 28.0 * std::f32::consts::TAU;\n                        project([at[0] + a.cos() * r, at[1], at[2] + a.sin() * r])\n                    })\n                    .collect();\n                if pts.len() == 28 {\n                    p.add(Shape::closed_line(pts, Stroke::new(sp.s(7.0), c(TEAL))));\n                }\n            }\n            Ui::WorldLabel { at, text: s } => {''')\nsub('engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs','''    /// Dev Mode's Win and Lose Now.''','''    /// What the mouse points at on the island.\n    pub pointing: Option<(Vec3, String)>,\n    /// Dev Mode's Win and Lose Now.''')\nsub('engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs','''        forced_score: None,''','''        pointing: None,\n        forced_score: None,''')\nI='engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/island.rs'\nsub(I,'''        // Hand input.\n        let stick = input.move_dir;''','''        // What the mouse points at gets a ring, and can be clicked.\n        self.pointing = input.aim.and_then(|aim| spots.iter().filter(|(_, p, _)| flat(*p - aim) < 1.2).min_by(|a, b| flat(a.1 - aim).total_cmp(&flat(b.1 - aim))).map(|s| (s.1, s.2.clone())));\n        // Hand input.\n        let stick = input.move_dir;''')\nMn='engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/menus.rs'\nsub(Mn,'''        if let Some((_, at, label)) = &self.near {''','''        if let Some((at, label)) = &self.pointing {\n            b.items.push(Ui::WorldRing { at: at.to_array(), r: 0.9 });\n            if self.near.as_ref().is_none_or(|n| n.2 != *label) {\n                b.items.push(Ui::WorldPrompt { at: (*at + Vec3::Y * 2.0).to_array(), glyph: Glyph::Confirm, label: label.clone() });\n            }\n        }\n        if let Some((_, at, label)) = &self.near {''')\nL='engine/crates/pav_app/src/fit_link.rs'\nsub(L,'''        f.aim = rig.ground_point(cursor, size, 0.0);''','''        f.aim = if self.mouse_last { rig.ground_point(cursor, size, 0.0) } else { None };''')\nsub(L,'''        f.song_pos = self.song_pos;\n        f''','''        f.song_pos = self.song_pos;\n        if self.hub_ended {\n            // The hub has called the end: the game takes no more input.\n            f = InputFrame { held: f.held & btn::HUB_GO, ..Default::default() };\n        }\n        f''')\nH='tests/hub.py'\nsub(H,'''            t0 = time.time()\n            done = False\n            while time.time() - t0 < 240:\n                if page.evaluate(\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\"):\n                    done = True\n                    break\n                page.wait_for_timeout(500)''','''            t0 = time.time()\n            done = False\n            ghosts = 0\n            while time.time() - t0 < 240:\n                if page.evaluate(\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\"):\n                    done = True\n                    break\n                for fr in page.frames:\n                    try:\n                        ghosts = max(ghosts, fr.evaluate(\"window.__hub ? Object.keys(window.__hub.ghosts).length : 0\"))\n                    except Exception:\n                        pass\n                page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n            check(f\"{name}: other players' ghosts arrive\", ghosts >= 1, ghosts)''')\nPY\ngrep -n \"fn closed_line\\|closed_line\" engine/crates/pav_ui/src/*.rs | head -2\ncat > README.md <<'E'\n# We Stand: dev folder\n\nA balance-and-wellness comedy on a resort of talking gym equipment, built on the Pavilion engine.\nThe plan is `../PLAN.md`; decisions it left open are in `notes/decisions.md`.\n\n- `engine/`: the engine with the game in it. The game is `crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`.\n- `tools/`: `build.sh` makes the single HTML; `gen_props.py`, `gen_sets.py` and `gen_clips.py` first drew the props, set maps and hand-keyed clips (their outputs are plain data, editable by hand); `make_page.py` and `page.template.html` make the page; `shots.sh` takes screenshots.\n- `tests/`: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]` prints failures and one line of counts. `tests/dev/` holds the screen tours and timing probes.\n- `hub/`: the AI Hub client and harness, as downloaded.\n\n## Numbers and words, with no rebuild\nRun the tools from `engine/`, and these are read from disk at each `load`: `games/fit/rules.toml` (every balance number; ranges and help in `rules.rs`, which also makes Dev Mode's sliders), `games/fit/charts.toml`, `games/fit/sets/*.toml`. `script.toml` holds every word and is read once per run. In the game, Pause > Dev Mode has live sliders, jumps, cheats and time controls.\n\n```\ncd engine\ncargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav\n./target/debug/pav capture scene=fit/event/tide ticks=120 width=1280 height=720 out=out.png\nprintf 'load scene=fit\\nplay bot=true ticks=6000\\ncapture out=out.png\\n' | ./target/debug/pav repl\n```\nDoors for tools and tests: `fit`, `fit/medley`, `fit/event/<name>`, `fit/stand`, `fit/stand/<phase>`, `fit/day/<n>`, `fit/free`, `fit/credits`.\n\n## Add an event\n1. A file in `games/fit/events/`: a state struct with `start`, `tick`, `bot`, `hud`, `score`. `breath.rs` is the shortest pattern.\n2. A line in `EvKind` and in the `Ev`, `each!` and `ALL_EVENTS` lists in `events/mod.rs` (its key, name, day, set, lane).\n3. A group of numbers in `rules.rs` (`group!`), added to `Rules` and `GROUPS`.\n4. A goal and how-to in `run.rs`, and a mat: a `MATS` entry in `tools/gen_sets.py` (or a `mat_<key>` spot and object by hand in `sets/hub.toml`).\n5. `tests/fit.rs` then checks it by itself: the bot must earn 2 stars, idling under 1. Add it to `ATTRACT` to show it in the demo.\n\n## Add a set\nA room file in `games/fit/sets/`, with a `[game] spots` table of named places and the `[view]` recipe (see any set). Add it to `SETS` in `mod.rs` and give it a number in `events/mod.rs`. Set origins are placed in code, 400 m apart: write coordinates from the map's corner.\n\n## Add a song\nA `const Song` in `pav_audio/src/music.rs`: BPM, steps per beat, chord roots per bar, and tracks of a patch and a pattern (semitones above the chord root, `R` for a rest). Give it a number in `song()` and `SONG_IDS`. `SimEvent::Music { song }` plays it. Sounds are the same idea in `fit_sfx`, by number in `games/fit/mod.rs`.\n\n## Add words, a clip or a prop\nWords: `script.toml`. A line may begin `Speaker: `. Clips: `anim/fit.json` (`anim_reload` and `animsheet` in `pav repl` show them with no rebuild). Props: format-2 JSON in `assets/props/lib/core/`; rebuild `pav` to see a new one.\nE\ncd engine; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 cargo check --locked -p pav_core -p pav_ui 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A7 | cut -c1-170 | head -20; cd ..; tail -12 notes/feedback.md; cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'E'\n- All systems in. Remaining: final exit interview, tools/build.sh, tests/run.sh all, 1080p file:// look, cleanup (engine/target, engine/.git, notes/cap, tests/dev outputs).\nE","description":"Add highlight ring, hub end handling, handle size, hub ghost check and README","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_read_input_tokens":638749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformati