{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjV2SdQPfdAjSwxbxeAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last rebuild passes the full suite, **87 passed, 0 failed**, and `tests/dev/handin_check.py` now passes all 12 of its checks against TASK.md and PLAN.md. That script quotes TASK.md's hand-in lines and parses its required fields, so the check doesn't rest on my own summary. The one FAIL on its first run was a bug in the script, which I fixed.\n\n**What the check confirms:**\n- **Files:** the game HTML and dev subfolder have the names TASK.md specifies, and `exit-interview.json` sits beside the HTML.\n- **Exit interview:** all 15 Source Information fields are filled, and `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". The feedback answers match the question counts (4, 6 and 4), and every `aiHub` field is filled.\n- **About screen:** the data in the page matches the exit interview exactly.\n- **Hub client:** it's pasted byte for byte, in the first script in the page.\n- **Plan content:** all 21 planned hand-keyed clips exist and are played. All the library props are placed; I added the fence and round table in this last pass.\n\n**Library clip not played directly:** `MESH2MOTION/Pushup`. As the plan directs, the plank pose is built from one of its frames.\n\n**Still different from the plan (the reasons are in `notes/plan-audit.md`):**\n- The Schedule uses tabs with rows instead of a carousel.\n- The arm flail only appears when no held clip is using the arms.\n- Tray Trek's own walk uses `FIT/CarryTray`; a guest on the island does the `Balance_Walk`.\n- Guests have 8 lines each, not 8 per day.\n- Some files the plan named are folded into others.\n- Prompt tests use the prompt function and a page field, not the Headless reading.\n\n**Limits of this evidence:**\n- `notes/plan-audit.md` is my own section-by-section reading of the plan. Only the items above were checked by script or test; the rest is my judgement.\n- 