{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjWawPniwxZeSgXEBoSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**We Stand** is done, and the final page passes everything: **90 checks passed, 0 failed**, and the hand-in check passes all 12 of its items. No planned clip or library prop is left unused.\n\nThe 90 comes from two runs on the same page. In the full run, core and hub had no failures (45 passed), but 6 browser checks failed because the machine was heavily loaded (load average around 50). Two fixed waits in my tests caused those failures, so I made them poll and reran the browser suite on its own: 45 passed.\n\n**Closed since my last message:**\n- The Schedule is now a real carousel of pavilions, followed by the events. I checked it in a screenshot.\n- The arm flail now takes over from held clips past a lean of 0.75, except during dives, where leaning is the control.\n- Marjorie has 8 lines per day.\n- A guest plays `Pushup`.\n- Prompts are now also tested through the Headless reading.\n\n**Two differences from the plan remain, both deliberate:**\n- **Tray Trek's walk:** it uses `FIT/CarryTray` instead of `Balance_Walk` plus an upper-body clip. The walk is driven by position and the engine has one clip slot, so the legs would stand still. A guest on the island does the `Balance_Walk`.\n- **File layout:** `intent.rs`, `medley.rs` and `attract.rs` are folded into `mod.rs`, `run.rs` and `menus.rs`, and `weblink.rs` is called `fit_link.rs`. Behaviour is the same and it's covered by the tests.\n\n**About the stop hook's objection:** I read `TASK.md` and `PLAN.md` in full at the start of this session, and the section-by-section result is in `notes/plan-audit.md`. That audit is still my own reading of the plan. Only the items that `tests/dev/handin_check.py` and the test suite cover have been checked mechanically.\n\n**Can't be done on this computer:** nobody has played the game or listened to it, and it hasn't run on a real controller, phone, TV or GPU. Feel and difficulty are still estimates.\n\nThe Source Information and all feedback are in my reply three messages back, and they're also on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`. The only out-of-date details are small: that reply's \"Still different\" points are now closed apart from the two above, and the test faults found after it are logged in `notes/feedback.md`, not in the exit interview.\n\nEverything is in `work/`; open `WeStand-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953.html` to play."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":728018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":982},"output_tokens":724,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb437ba7-0477-4143-bb04-ff33f49efd62","uuid":"39fbc7d5-bcb7-4e47-8894-c5688fe706b9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:02:56.750Z","request_id":"req_011CgjWaw1xYJsiCppk3qbpq"}
