{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ctc33u1Bh7sb9H1yyHaUig","type":"tool_result","content":"=== TASK.md, requirements\nSOURCE: Wii Fit\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/blob/main/START_HERE.md, making a new game on its engine. You may change anything in it, the engine included, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs. The rest of the t\n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\n\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953].html in root when you’\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after chan\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL f\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (in\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, bu\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:39:53\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits scre\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything \n\n=== PLAN.md 18, finishing and brief map\n## 18. Finishing\n\n1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`\n2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The A\n3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\n4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\n5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\n\n### What each brief item maps to\n\n| Brief item | Section |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective | 1 |\n| Title method | 0, 17 |\n| Research | Optional. The plan already reflects a short web search on Wii Fit, and that is enough; report what you actually did |\n| Single HTML package | 14, 15, 18 (no external dependencies are needed) |\n| Build on the engine, change anything | 14 |\n| Art direction, new assets, library for generics | 8 |\n| Animation | 9 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | 10, 16 |\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 13, 16 |\n| Dev folder, bundling, shared machine, ports and processes | 0, 15, 16; your brief has the rules |\n| Performance out of scope, as much detail as the scene needs | 8, 15 |\n| One test command, scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review agents | 16 |\n| Stand-ins: pad, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | 15, 16 |\n| Original game, feature-complete vertical slice, extendable with normal tools | 1, 14 (all data in TOML, JSON clips and props; `README.md` explains adding an event, a set and a song) |\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | 11 |\n| Attract mode | 12 |\n| Narrative tone | 7 |\n| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, glyphs, Xbox option, no dense screens | 3, 11 |\n| Touch-only behaviour | 11, 12 |\n| No TODOs or stubs | 16, 17 |\n| Source Information and all feedback in chat and on About, exit interview | 11, 14, 18 |\n\n=== folder\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    63641 Nov  4 22:39 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     1566 Nov  5 02:02 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha      219 Nov  4 22:39 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    12564 Nov  4 22:39 TASK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha     4096 Nov  5 00:06 WeStand-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 12254825 Nov  5 01:45 WeStand-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-223953.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     6754 Nov  5 00:56 exit-interview.json\nWeStand-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-202611