{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjcBTxLtyewtcMa1u9qy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**We Stand** is finished, and no difference from the plan's Tray Trek clips remains. On the final page, the full run gives **88 passed, 0 failed**, and the hand-in check passes all 12 items.\n\n**Tray Trek:** `FIT/CarryTray` is now `Balance_Walk`'s own legs with arms holding the tray, built into one clip. That gives the plan's combination with the engine's single clip slot, and the capture in `notes/tray-final.png` shows it working.\n\n**Both documents:** I read `TASK.md` in full and all 633 lines of `PLAN.md` again in the last two turns, so those reads are now in this conversation.\n\n**Gaps I know of:**\n- **\"Ghosts match by area\" (PLAN.md section 16):** this has no direct test, because the filter runs only in the browser build. The hub harness shows other players' ghost data arriving, not that they're drawn only in the matching event.\n- **Number differences:** PLAN.md section 0 calls its numbers starting values, and a few of mine differ. Tray Trek pays 180 per glass plus a 100 bonus, not 200 per glass, so a perfect run tops out at exactly 1000. My Balance Core test also allows more idle wander than the plan's target, and I didn't measure the actual figure.\n- **Breath Bloom and Tempo Squats scoring:** these formulas differ from the plan on purpose, because the plan's versions gave idle play a star. That's noted in `notes/decisions.md`.\n- **The plan audit:** `notes/plan-audit.md` is still my own reading, so anything beyond the tests and `tests/dev/handin_check.py` rests on my judgement.\n- **Can't be done on this computer:** a person playing or listening to it, and a real controller, phone, TV or GPU.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback are in my earlier reply, on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`; the issue count there is now about 20, and only the \"Still different\" notes in that re